  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green education for sustainable agriculture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project assesses the potential of geothermal energy as a sustainable heating solution for greenhouse operations at the Busk site, in the Lviv region of Ukraine. This assessment provides critical information on the availability and viability of geothermal resources, helping agricultural producers to understand whether the region can support sustainable heating solutions for their operations. In doing so, the study will also identify any regulatory or environmental considerations that may impact the development and operation of geothermal systems. By addressing these factors early on, private companies (local and international) can identify and mitigate risks, ensure compliance and ultimately create a more robust and sustainable investment strategy in the greenhouse sector of Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
